biểu nào của HRW sau ngày 10/12/2025". One exception, in Findings below.

**The decree trap is not sprung.** Line 39 says the law *delegates* criteria, scope and
duration to implementing decrees and then says "hồ sơ nghiên cứu không xác định được
tình trạng ban hành các nghị định này" — it does **not** say the decrees have not been
issued. This is precisely the conversion the axis was told to hunt for, and the piece
declines it.

**B-ceiling declared in plain body prose, not only in the table.** Line 7, in the body,
before any substance: no source was opened, egress was blocked, no claim is grade A,
all capped at B. Restated in the method note at line 66. Requirement met.

**Grades:** all 20 table rows are B. No A anywhere; no C or D leaked in. Two rows carry
an explicit "khoảng trống thông tin, không phải bằng chứng của sự im lặng" qualifier on
the grade, which is the correct treatment for a non-finding.

**Scope and plan (`00-brief.md`):** five movements as planned (Mở → Thay đổi thực chất
→ Ba phía tranh cãi → Lý do chính thức → Điều đáng theo dõi) plus the confidence table;
the locked lexicon is respected throughout; the body is **inside the 950–1,300 band**
(count and method below). The brief's published deviations (Gates 1 and 2 skipped, eval
run) are declared in `00-brief.md` itself, not concealed. No scope drift: the piece
stays on one statute and reaches for the PDPL, Decree 147 and the 2018 law only to keep
them apart — exactly the licence `00-brief.md` L15-16 grants.

**Word count, measured independently.** No shell is available to me, so I counted by
hand, paragraph by paragraph. Body prose, headings and standalone punctuation tokens
excluded: **≈1,224 words** (margin ±3%). Reconstructing the receipts' own
whitespace-token method for comparison — prose 1,224 + ~28 standalone em-dash/hyphen
tokens + ~51 heading words + 6 Markdown markers ≈ **1,309 tokens** — against their
measured 1,305. The two independent counts agree to ~0.3%, and both are inside the
band on either definition.

**Tense/currency:** the piece ships 2026-09-01, after the 1/7/2026 commencement. I found
**no obligation written as forthcoming**: the localisation, takedown and cross-border
provisions are stated in unmarked present ("phải đặt…", "luật quy định thời hạn…"), and
the closing explicitly refers to "các nghĩa vụ **đã có hiệu lực**". No tense defect.

